<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">19th Route Army</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1930">1930</a>–<a href="/years/1934">1934</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The 19th Route Army was a Chinese Nationalist army from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangdong">Guangdong</a> that won fame defending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanghai">Shanghai</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in the January 28 Incident of 1932. Moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fujian">Fujian</a>, its commanders rebelled in 1933 against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek">Chiang Kai-shek</a>'s policy of appeasing Japan and set up the Fujian People's Government. Government forces crushed the rebellion in early 1934 and the army was disbanded.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/19th-route-army.jpg" alt="19th Route Army" width="320" height="206" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:General_Cai_Ting-kai,_the_commander_of_the_19th_Route_Army,_encouraging_his_men_in_the_first_line_of_the_battle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
